## Status / re-proof trigger
- **as-run build predates the bus-accessor commit** (`board::leaf_i2c`/`console_uart_*`), which is a
  **behaviour-preserving** refactor for the console (same eUSCI_A1, same P4.2/3 pins, same clock).
  So the observed behaviour applies to HEAD, but a **single-adapter reflash of HEAD** is the pending
  re-proof to make this artifact match the current tree exactly. Re-proof is blocked while two eZ-FET
  adapters are attached (multi-adapter JTAG guard) — do it with only the FR2355 connected.
- Not yet proven here (future): the SBW boot-record channel (`bootrec.rs` is dormant/unwired) and the
  Tier-2 SoM-mastered I²C/UART acceptance (full bench). This log is Tier-1 (dev-board) console proof.
